# DealMemory Client SDK & Integration Guide

DealMemory provides lightweight client libraries for web browsers, Node.js runtimes, Python applications, and direct HTTP clients. All clients implement **privacy-first edge sanitization**, **idempotent delivery**, and **automatic offline queuing**.

The simplest integration path is the same one used across the product: one package, one key, one init command.

---

## The simplest path

On the customer app side, that looks like this:

```bash
npm install dealmemory
npx dealmemory init

# .env
DEALMEMORY_API_KEY=pk_live_your_project_key
```

After that, `import 'dealmemory/auto'` starts tracking page views, clicks, sessions, and common product milestones automatically. The CLI writes the bootstrap into the app for you, and the SDK reads everything it needs from the environment.

---

## Quick integration (cURL & fetch)

No external libraries are required to send product actions to DealMemory. You can emit events directly over standard HTTP POST requests.

### JavaScript (Native `fetch`)

```typescript
const event = {
  id: crypto.randomUUID(),
  projectKey: 'pk_live_your_project_key',
  name: 'trial_started',
  userId: 'user_98721',
  anonymousId: 'anon_34291',
  sessionId: crypto.randomUUID(),
  occurredAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  properties: {
    plan: 'pro_trial',
    referrer: 'github'
  }
};

const response = await fetch('https://your-dealmemory-host.com/api/v1/events/batch', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'x-project-key': 'pk_live_your_project_key'
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ events: [event] })
});

const result = await response.json();
console.log('Ingestion result:', result);
```

### cURL

```bash
curl 'https://your-dealmemory-host.com/api/v1/events/batch' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'x-project-key: pk_live_your_project_key' \
  --data '{
    "events": [
      {
        "id": "c71a39f0-2bf7-4e94-9844-3d024b819f71",
        "projectKey": "pk_live_your_project_key",
        "name": "integration_connected",
        "userId": "user_123",
        "occurredAt": "2026-10-28T12:00:00Z",
        "properties": {
          "provider": "github"
        }
      }
    ]
  }'
```

