## TypeScript / JavaScript SDK

The DealMemory TypeScript SDK is in `packages/sdk` and can be imported into web apps, React, Next.js, Vue, or Node.js services.

### Installation

```bash
npm install dealmemory
```

That is the whole install. Drop your key in `.env` and let the CLI wire it up — no project id, no apiUrl, no config file anywhere:

```bash
# .env
DEALMEMORY_API_KEY=pk_live_your_project_key

# writes the tracking bootstrap into your entry file
npx dealmemory init
```

### Initializing the client

```typescript
// Zero-config: the CLI already wrote this import into your app
import 'dealmemory/auto';

// Need custom events? The shared client is exported for you:
import { track, identify } from 'dealmemory/auto';
identify('user_94812');
track('repository_connected', { provider: 'github' });
```

Prefer an explicit client? Every option is optional — only override when you self-host or need privacy controls:

```typescript
import { DealMemory } from 'dealmemory';

export const dm = new DealMemory({
  projectKey: 'pk_live_your_project_key',
  apiUrl: 'https://your-dealmemory-host.com/api',
  flushIntervalMs: 5000,
  autoCapture: true,
  privacy: {
    captureQueryString: false,
    blockedEvents: ['internal_healthcheck']
  }
});
```

### Identifying users

```typescript
dm.identify('user_94812', {
  company: 'Acme Corp',
  role: 'Engineering Lead'
});
```

### Tracking product milestones

```typescript
dm.track('repository_connected', {
  repoName: 'dealmemory-core',
  branchCount: 4
});

dm.setGoal('deploy_first_agent');
dm.trialStarted();
dm.firstValueReached();
dm.checkoutStarted();
dm.checkoutCompleted();
dm.integrationConnected({ provider: 'slack' });
```

### Resetting sessions

```typescript
dm.reset();
```

