## Edge privacy & credential redaction

DealMemory enforces zero-trust privacy rules at both the client SDK level and the server ingestion endpoint.

### Patterns blocked and sanitized

Any event property containing strings matching these patterns is rejected or redacted:

```regex
(?:pk_live|sk_live|whsec)_[a-zA-Z0-9_]{16,}
\bBearer(?:\s|%20)+[a-zA-Z0-9_\-\.~+/]{16,}={0,2}
\beyJ[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}
-----BEGIN[ A-Z0-9_-]*PRIVATE KEY-----
(?:password|token|secret)\s*=\s*['"]?[^\s'";&]{3,}['"]?
```

### Property key restrictions

Property keys containing keywords such as `password`, `token`, `secret`, `message`, `text`, or `value` are automatically excluded.

### URL sanitization

All page URLs and referrers have query parameters (`?code=...`, `?token=...`) and hash fragments stripped before submission.

